  "description": "One man has spent thirty years redesigning football. After an injury ended his career, Laurențiu Ginghină concluded the rules themselves were at fault — too much running, too many collisions — and has been revising them ever since, explaining octagonal pitches to indulgent officials. A deadpan documentary about systems-thinking as a life's consolation: the local instance of a universal type.\n\nThey talk about the beautiful game, but for Laurentiu Ginghina, it's not enough. Football must be modified, streamlined, freed from restraints; corners are to be rounded off, players assigned to zones and subteams, norms revised. ...",
